# 🧪 6. Real-World Compliance Scenarios

## **Scenario 1 — User Cannot Access Teams**
**Cause:** Device non-compliant due to missing OS updates.  
**Fix:** Update OS → Sync device → Access restored.  
**Ticket Note:** Device non-compliant due to outdated OS. Guided user through updates. Compliance restored.

---

## **Scenario 2 — Device Marked Non-Compliant After Password Change**
**Cause:** Device token expired.  
**Fix:** Sign out → Sign in → Sync device.  
**Ticket Note:** Device token expired after password reset. User re-authenticated and synced. Compliance restored.

---

## **Scenario 3 — Android Device Blocked**
**Cause:** Play Protect disabled.  
**Fix:** Enable Play Protect → Sync.  
**Ticket Note:** Android non-compliant due to Play Protect disabled. Enabled and synced. Access restored.

---

## **Scenario 4 — macOS Device Not Receiving Compliance Policies**
**Cause:** User not in assignment group.  
**Fix:** Add user → Sync device.  
**Ticket Note:** macOS device missing compliance profile due to group assignment. Added user and synced.

